---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Masonic Architecture: Operative & Speculative Transmission | Hub V"
  description="Explore the operative and speculative origins of Freemasonry. Decode how the tools of the builder conceal profound psychological technologies."
>
  <main class="site-wrapper section theme-affirming" style="padding-top: 40px;">
      
    <!-- WAYFINDING CONDUIT -->
    <nav class="shsq-wayfinding-conduit reveal" aria-label="Hub Navigation" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto 50px auto; padding: 0 20px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px;">
      <ul class="breadcrumb-trail" style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; gap: 10px; font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem;">
        <li><a href="/the-escape-matrix/">&#8629; Master Grid</a></li>
        <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--shsq-muted);">/</li>
        <li class="current-node" aria-current="page" style="color: var(--shsq-parchment);">Hub V: Masonic Architecture</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="adjacent-node">
        <a href="/occult-history/" style="font-family: var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 1px; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; padding-bottom: 2px;">Engage Hub VI &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- HUB HERO -->
    <header class="shsq-hub-hero reveal" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 60px; max-width: 1200px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 20px;">
      <span class="archive-eyebrow" style="color: var(--shsq-silver); font-size: 0.95rem; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 15px;">Hub V &middot; The Temple Builders</span>
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); margin: 0 0 25px 0; line-height: 1.1;">Masonic Architecture</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--shsq-parchment); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
        Explore the operative and speculative origins of Freemasonry. Decode the esoteric transmission of the Craft from the medieval building guilds through the Scottish and York Rites, revealing how the tools of the builder and the geometry of the lodge conceal profound psychological and spiritual technologies required to construct the immortal Astral Body.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- PILLAR CLUSTER GRID (6 NODES) -->
    <div class="shsq-cluster-grid reveal reveal-delay-1" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 30px; margin-bottom: 80px; max-width: 1200px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 20px;">
        
      <!-- Pillar 1 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 1: The Blue Lodge</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">From Operative to Speculative</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Trace the historical transition of the Craft from physical stone-masonry into a philosophical system of morality, veiled in allegory and illustrated by the working tools of the Entered Apprentice and Fellowcraft.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/operative-to-speculative/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Pillar 2 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 2: The Master Mason</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Legend of Hiram Abiff</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Deconstruct the central mythology of the Third Degree. Analyze the murder of the Chief Architect as a mechanical allegory for the loss of spiritual light and the psychological necessity of somatic resurrection.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/legend-of-hiram-abiff/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Pillar 3 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 3: The York Rite</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Royal Arch &amp; The Lost Word</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Investigate Capitular Masonry and the mythos of the Secret Vault. Discover how the recovery of the "Lost Word" completes the Master Mason degree and symbolizes the ultimate realization of Divine Truth.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/royal-arch-lost-word/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Pillar 4 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 4: The Scottish Rite</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">Morals and Dogma</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Examine the monumental synthesis of Albert Pike, who expanded the Masonic architecture into thirty-three degrees, embedding the deepest mechanics of the Kabbalah, Hermeticism, and Zoroastrianism into the Craft.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/morals-and-dogma-pike/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Pillar 5 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 5: Temple Physics</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">Tracing Boards &amp; Geometry</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Decode the visual ciphers of the Masonic Lodge. Understand how the Square, the Compasses, and the Letter 'G' function not merely as emblems, but as cognitive maps for organizing the human psyche.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/tracing-boards-geometry/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Pillar 6 -->
      <article class="shsq-cluster-card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
        <span class="silo-eyebrow">Pillar 6: The Esoteric Fraternities</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">Rosicrucian &amp; Templar Interference</h3>
        <p style="flex-grow: 1; margin-bottom: 35px;">
          Uncover the historical intersections between the original Craft lodges and higher-order esoteric societies, detailing how Templar chivalry and Rosicrucian alchemy infiltrated the Masonic bloodstream.
        </p>
        <a href="/masonic-architecture/templar-rosicrucian-masonry/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="align-self: flex-start;">
          Enter the Source &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

    </div>

    <!-- TERMINAL PROMPT -->
    <aside class="shsq-terminal-prompt reveal" aria-labelledby="terminal-heading" style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto 80px auto; text-align: center;">
      <h2 id="terminal-heading">The Lodge is Tiled</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--shsq-parchment); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 700px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        The architectural blueprints for the inner Temple have been laid out. By learning the tools of the Builder, the Theurgist prepares to square the rough ashlar of the biological self. You may now advance to the historical manifestation of these forces.
      </p>
      <a href="/occult-history/" class="btn btn-primary">
        Engage Hub VI &#8599;
      </a>
    </aside>

    <footer class="shsq-footer-note reveal reveal-delay-2" style="text-align: center; color: var(--shsq-silver); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.2); padding-top: 30px; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px;">
      <p style="margin: 0;">History SQ: Decoding the Enneagrammatic Escape Plan &middot; Guided by Sophia Mysterion.</p>
    </footer>

  </main>
</Layout>